<title>PORTUGAL: PRESS DIGEST - Portugal -- Feb 20.</title>
<headline>PRESS DIGEST - Portugal -- Feb 20.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following are leading domestic stories in Portuguese newspapers.</p>
<p>PUBLICO</p>
<p>- Celebrated poet Antonio Gedeao died in a Lisbon hospital.</p>
<p>- Politicians prepare for debate on changes to abortion law.</p>
<p>DIARIO DE NOTICIAS</p>
<p>- Greenpeace demonstrators prevented a U.S. ship carrying gene-modified maize from docking at a Lisbon harbour.</p>
<p>DIARIO ECONOMICO</p>
<p>- A public offer to exchange shares will be required in the restructuring of ship repairer Lisnave.</p>
<p>- A senior governmment official tells the paper that the budget deficit could be below 2.9 percent this year.</p>
<p>--Lisbon bureau 3511-3538254</p>
